extraction_notes: |
  Read from Rifts World Book 6: South America printed 111-112 (cache
  p112-p113), text layer checked against a 200 dpi render of printed 112. The
  class begins at the foot of printed 111 (the Flying Tiger''s skills and
  equipment fill the top of that page) and ends on printed 112; printed 113 is
  the Hunter Cat. No flame-panther class, and no class named Flame Panther,
  was in production on 2026-09-25.

  1. XP_TABLE is the "Flame Panther, Flying Tiger & Oracle Cat" ladder in the
     experience tables, printed 168 (cache p169). Lower bounds stored as
     printed: 0, 2,201, 4,401, 8,801, 18,001, 26,001, 36,001, 52,001, 72,001,
     97,001, 132,001, 182,001, 232,001, 282,001, 343,001.
  2. POOLS: hit points P.E. x2 plus 1D6 per level. S.D.C. 1D4x100+100 is a
     racial S.D.C. and is stored as a pool bonus, not sdc_base. The M.D.C. line
     is the Flame Aura''s (70 +10 per level) and exists only while the aura is
     up, so it is in the Flame Aura ability and not mdc_base. The class states
     neither sdc_base nor mdc_base; it is a race, so men_of_arms: false. No
     P.P.E. is printed and none is stored.
  3. HORROR FACTOR 9 is stored; the 14 with the aura on is prose.
  4. PSIONICS: master psionic, I.S.P. M.E. + 3D4x10, +10 per level. Three
     powers from each of Sensitive, Healing and Physical: nine starting picks
     in three groups. The book prints no further psionic powers by level and
     none are scheduled. The pyrokinetic powers are the race''s own and are
     abilities, as the Burster''s are, not catalog psionic rows; the catalog''s
     Impervious to Fire row was not granted because this version differs
     (one-tenth damage from M.D. fire, half from electricity).
  5. BONUSES: the book prints none beyond +1 to strike with the flame bolt,
     which is conditional and in that ability''s text.
  6. ROCKET JUMP: the ink reads "difficult (3 to strike)" with no sign; stored
     as -3, since a penalty is plainly meant.
  7. SKILLS: Basic Math is Mathematics: Basic 45+10; Lore: Demons and Monsters
     is Lore: Demons & Monsters 25+10; Language: Spanish 50+30; Ancient
     Egyptian has no catalog row and is a fixed Language: Other at 50+30; one
     language of choice +10%; Land Navigation 36+10; Tracking: Humans and
     Monsters is Tracking (people) 25+15; First Aid 45+15; Wilderness
     Survival 30+10; Prowl 25+10; W.P. Energy Rifle; two W.P.s of choice. No
     literacy is printed and none was added.
  8. HAND TO HAND: Expert, changeable to Martial Arts for one other skill. The
     Flame Panther''s line prints no Assassin option (the Flying Tiger''s, just
     above it on the same page, does), so only martial_arts is priced.
  9. RELATED SKILLS: the book prints its own R.C.C. related ("other") skills,
     four plus one at levels 3, 7, 11 and 15, and pairs the race with no
     O.C.C., so they are stored as occ_related_skills (as the Amazon''s are).
     Communications +10; Domestic, Electrical, Military, Physical, Pilot
     Related, W.P. any; Espionage, Rogue, Technical, Wilderness +5; Medical
     Holistic Medicine only +5; Pilot any +10. Mechanical and Science none.
     Horsemanship is granted because the catalog files riding under its own
     category and Pilot is any (the Amazon decision).
  10. SECONDARY: four, plus two at levels 2, 4, 8 and 12, from the same list
      without the bonuses.
  11. EQUIPMENT: energy rifle (Wilk''s laser rifle equivalent: the Wilk''s 447)
      or the Colombian RR-C40 Rocket Rifle; a blade weapon of choice and the
      light M.D.C. body armor (1D4x10+10 M.D.C.) are catalog choice sets, since
      the book names neither; survival kit.
  12. MONEY: 1D4x1000 credits in salable articles is trade goods, not coin, so
      starting_money is not stored; it is a restriction line.
